From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:42:53 +0200
Subject: wifi: brcmfmac: demote unexpected firmware channel message to debug

Firmware with ccode=ALL, such as on the AP6330, reports the Japan 4.9 GHz
channels 184-216. The driver skips them, but logs one error per channel
at every interface start. Log them at debug level.

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/cfg80211.c
@@ -7069,8 +7069,8 @@ static int brcmf_construct_chaninfo(struct brcmf_cfg80211_info *cfg,
 			/* It seems firmware supports some channel we never
 			 * considered. Something new in IEEE standard?
 			 */
-			bphy_err(drvr, "Ignoring unexpected firmware channel %d\n",
-				 ch.control_ch_num);
+			brcmf_dbg(INFO, "Ignoring unexpected firmware channel %d\n",
+				  ch.control_ch_num);
 			continue;
 		}
 
-- 
Armbian

